BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-hayy-cinema@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260618T060000Z
DTEND:20260715T150000Z
SUMMARY:Hayy Cinema | “Kef Hayyak?” 3rd Edition Screenings and Awards Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the screenings of the third edition of “Kef Hayyak?” cohort’s films! “Kef Hayyak?” is a unique documentary filmmaking challenge that invites aspiring filmmakers to capture the essence of their neighborhoods in Jeddah through their own lens—using only their phones. Building on the success of its first two editions\, the programme launched an open call for its third edition in December 2025\, selecting 13 projects for development based on the quality and originality of their creative proposals.
LOCATION:Hayy Jameel
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-hayy-cinema.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-hayy-cinema-2@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260701T060000Z
DTEND:20260715T150000Z
SUMMARY:Hayy Cinema | July 2026
DESCRIPTION:July 2026 At Hayy Cinema Join Hayy Cinema this July for a continuation of stories exploring identity\, memory\, and human connection\, with extended screenings of this season’s featured films. The lineup continues with A Matter of Life and Death (2025) \, a Saudi rom-com where fate\, fear\, and unlikely love collide\; The Stories (2025) \, a cross-cultural tale of connection through letters and shared humanity\; and You Will Die at Twenty (2019) \, in which a young man grows up under a prophecy that he will die at the...
LOCATION:Hayy Jameel
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-hayy-cinema-2.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-jameel-library@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260701T060000Z
DTEND:20260731T150000Z
SUMMARY:Jameel Library | July Community Programmes
DESCRIPTION:Join the Jameel Library for a wide range of programmes led by community members this July! You could also pitch your own programme here . Grotto’s Summer Reading Club To kick-off the Summer Reading Challenge\, the Jameel Library is hosting the cultural and literary initiative Grotto to lead curated book discussions dedicated to the interrogation of identity\, myth\, and historical endurance.
LOCATION:Hayy Jameel
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-jameel-library.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-jameel-library-summer-reading-challenge@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260701T060000Z
DTEND:20260831T150000Z
SUMMARY:Jameel Library | Summer Reading Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Jameel Library invites you to build a relationship with the library through curiosity\, discovery\, and spending time exploring its resources. This challenge celebrates the moments you spend here cultivating new interests and passions rather than the number of books you finish. Throughout July and August\, participants will receive prizes based on the number of hours they spend at Jameel Library\, turning every visit into a small seed planted among the shelves\, and nurtured with every new visit.
LOCATION:Hayy Jameel
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-jameel-library-summer-reading-challenge.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-hayy-explorers@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260702T060000Z
DTEND:20261001T150000Z
SUMMARY:Hayy Explorers | As Told by The Land: Traces & Memory
DESCRIPTION:As Told by the Land is a three-month long thematic programme at Hayy Explorers for children aged 6–15 years old. Through educational programmes and artist interventions\, it responds to the current Hayy Arts exhibitions by exploring themes of storytelling\, movement\, and shifting worlds. Across the three months\, children are invited to follow paths\, collect traces\, and construct new worlds from their immediate surroundings and everyday life.
LOCATION:Hayy Jameel
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-hayy-explorers.html
END:VEVENT
